      "text": "Since each row has 2 more cans than the previous row, this becomes a problem of finding the sum of an arithmetic series. The first term is the first row (1 can), the common difference is 2 cans, and the sum is 100 cans. The formula for an arithmetic series is: \\( S = \\frac{n}{2} (a_1 + a_n) \\), where \\( S \\) is the sum, \\( n \\) is the number of terms, \\( a_1 \\) is the first term, and \\( a_n \\) is the last term. For this problem, \\( S = 100 \\), \\( d = 2 \\), and \\( a_1 = 1 \\). We want to find \\( n \\).\n\nThe last term can be found using \\( a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d \\), so in this case, \\( a_n = 1 + (n-1)2 = 1 + 2n - 2 = 2n - 1 \\).\n\nPlugging the given values into the formula, we get:\n\\[ 100 = \\frac{n}{2} (1 + (2n - 1)) \\]\n\\[ 100 = \\frac{n}{2} \\cdot 2n \\]\n\\[ 100 = n^2 \\]\n\nTaking the square root of both sides:\n\\[ \\sqrt{100} = \\sqrt{n^2} \\]\n\\[ 10 = n \\]\n\nTherefore, the display contains \\(\\boxed{10}\\) rows.",
